## Euclidean Algorithm — GCD Explanation

---

## What is GCD?

```
GCD = Greatest Common Divisor
GCD(12, 8) = 4   ← biggest number that divides BOTH 12 and 8
GCD(10, 5) = 5
GCD(7,  3) = 1
```

---

## The Theorem

```
GCD(a, b) = GCD(a - b, b)    ← subtraction version
GCD(a, b) = GCD(a % b, b)    ← modulo version (FASTER)
```

### Why does this work?

```
GCD(48, 18)
= GCD(48 % 18, 18)
= GCD(12, 18)
= GCD(12, 18 % 12)
= GCD(12, 6)
= GCD(12 % 6, 6)
= GCD(0, 6)
= 6  ✅
```

When one number becomes **0**, the other is the **GCD**!

